      "date": "2026-11-26 10:00:15.000000000",
      "message": "Patch Set 1:\n\n(1 comment)\n\nAI code review results below, please doublecheck\n\nLooks good; the only inline item is a commit-message nit, so there's no need to re-spin for it alone.\n\nA question on coverage: cfg/local.sh evaluates MGSNID while init_test_env() runs, before load_modules(). formatall() then runs load_modules() only on the local node unless LOAD_MODULES_REMOTE=true, and that defaults to false. So on freshly booted servers, the first format still builds both --mgsnode and --failnode from the hostname -I guess. The LNet path only takes over once modules are loaded on those hosts, for example on a later reformat. Is that enough to cover the TLU-271 failure, or does that setup load LNet on the servers some other way?",
      "accounts_in_message": [],
      "_revision_number": 1
    }
  ],
