        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Minh Diep",
          "email": "mdiep@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-11-25 17:38:00.000000000",
          "tz": -480
        },
        "subject": "LU-21336 tests: ask LNet for a node's NIDs",
        "message": "LU-21336 tests: ask LNet for a node's NIDs\n\nh2name_or_ip() built a NID for each address from \"hostname -I\", so a\nnode with a second ethernet interface got NIDs that LNet does not\nlisten on, and a client given one as a target's failover peer retried\nit forever.\n\nUse host_nids_address(), which already asks LNet, and fall back to the\nold guess when the module is not loaded.  A literal IP still maps to a\nsingle NID for callers that want one rail.  Set LCTL before the config\nfile is sourced, since cfg/*.sh calls h2nettype.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nTLC-bug-id: TLU-271\nSigned-off-by: Robert Read <rread@thelustrecollective.com>\nSigned-off-by: Minh Diep <mdiep@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5\nChange-Id: Iafbe3d400634b74b10968e7df1b417ddc3454ca7\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
